 flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $48K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Remitly Global, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $4.8B market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +36% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -44% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $296M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.79\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -17.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 10.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.0933709483151556},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $12.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Remitly Global (NASDAQ:RELY) Releases Earnings Results, Beats Expectations By $0.15 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/remitly-global-nasdaqrely-releases-earnings-results-beats-expectations-by-0-15-eps.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793995007.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Remitly (RELY) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/remitly-rely-q3-2026-earnings-153012000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793893120.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"RELY Q3 Earnings Call Highlights Growth and Higher Outlook","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024405/rely-q3-earnings-call-hi